{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Bare places.</b> Some say it is like מתערב כאזרח רענן (like a native tree, flourishing) (Psalms 37:35), and its meaning is moist, and the sense is that every bare place that is on the Nile and at its mouth, and all seed of the Nile — everything will dry up. And some say: uncovered is everything that was on the Nile and at its mouth, for the vegetation is like a covering:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:15.191849444Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}